From 3cd12869f8576af96f21c3a362388b4edb4d981c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:10:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-4 C data planes

Add the six C-class batch-4 Units on top of the source-lock tree
(canonical + 0120-0129 + 0131 + 0134; the parallel batch-3 layers are not
required here). No guest evidence is recorded; host catalog keeps all six
planned.

- weight (U030): HX711 bit-pulse data plane. The model observes guest
  clock edges on yellow, shifts out the 24-bit fixture on white MSB-first,
  consumes the 1/3/2 gain pulses, then marks a conversion complete and
  re-arms DAT after a synthetic 100ms ready delay. Weighing mechanics and
  HX711 electrical behavior are NOT modeled; the product-page FAQ I2C
  wording conflicts with the PinMap/driver GPIO path and stays a blocker.
- bldc-driver (U181): CONTROL_BLDC at 0x65 with the official register
  file: mode, direction, motor model, pole pairs, int16le PWM, float/int/
  ASCII RPM and frequency views, 12-byte little-endian PID, flash-write
  counter, firmware and address migration. Motor electrical behavior,
  stall protection and the 5V output are NOT modeled.
- ac-measure (U164): US_ACMEASURE at 0x42 deriving the documented ASCII
  string views (fixed model-side width convention) and little-endian byte
  views from the same fixtures, plus coefficients, save-coefficient,
  data-ready, firmware and address migration. AC 100-240V@10A is a
  measurement input and is NEVER modeled as a switchable load; mains,
  isolation and metering accuracy are NOT RUN.
- dds (U105): CONTROL_DDS at 0x31 encoding the AD9833 mode/control/frequency
  (28-bit, 10MHz reference) and phase (11-bit) words with the dual
  register selection bits; analog waveform/amplitude are NOT modeled.
- gps (U032): UART NMEA fixture injection. A 50ms timer feeds one
  ';'-separated fixture sentence into the guest UART RX path when the
  firmware routes UART RX to the white pin; without a guest route nothing
  is injected. GNSS RF/satellite behavior and checksum validation are NOT
  modeled.
- uhf-rfid (U107): JRD4035 UART frame capture/injection. Guest 0xBB..0x7E
  command frames are captured on yellow; each complete frame triggers the
  next ';'-separated hex response fixture on white when routed. RF/Gen2
  air protocol and kill-lock/password security are NOT modeled.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 board, no guest firmware) validates property
registration, fixture read/write, range/read-only rejection and defaults;
it is not a functional PASS.
